Initial same-number replay/observer comparison failed its 1e-6 q-alignment assertion. A -3..+3 offset comparison found that replay frame t matches observer sample t+1 to within 5e-10 in q over the audited window; same-number samples can differ by as much as 0.10648 in a joint coordinate. The final analysis uses that measured one-step offset and lane 1, rather than silently pairing same-number records.
